WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.571
Binary search applies whenever a feasibility check flips once from false to true across sorted candidates.

00:00:07.571 --> 00:00:14.286
Instead of searching only inside an explicit array, search over the space of possible answers.

00:00:14.286 --> 00:00:19.000
Verify that if a capacity works, every larger capacity also works.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.418
Keep one pointer strictly on the invalid side and the other on the valid side.

00:00:25.418 --> 00:00:29.794
Halve the interval until the pointers sit on adjacent integers.

00:00:29.794 --> 00:00:34.240
Clear invariants eliminate off-by-one errors and infinite loops.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.873
Python's bisect module locates insertion points in compiled C speed.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:48.154
Use bisect_left for the first index at least the target, and bisect_right for the first index strictly greater.

00:00:48.154 --> 00:00:53.600
Subtracting the two indices counts exact occurrences in logarithmic time.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:01:01.241
When binary searching floating-point coordinates, a while-loop on epsilon can stall due to precision limits.

00:01:01.241 --> 00:01:04.861
Run a fixed loop of sixty to eighty iterations instead.

00:01:04.861 --> 00:01:08.744
Each step halves the interval and guarantees high accuracy.
